TITLE:Scanner Spec
H1:M7 · The scanner and diagnosing (Day 5, Halloran, with Torres's old scanner) <span class="draft">spec for approval</span>
SUB:Your first tool. Inspecting a faulty machine with the diagnostic scanner shows its parts with a reading each; you pick the part to fetch. Before the scanner, inspecting simply tells you the part (as now). Step 2, sub-block 24g, now with the head-scratcher seat (it opens the same day as your first head-scratcher, and both are Torres's). Plan Part 2, M7.
NAV:plain=In plain words|day=Day 5|panel=The panel|wrong=A wrong pick|grow=How it grows|b=Builder|save=Save|tests=Tests|ranges=Builds and keys|faq=FAQ

<p class="note"><b>Approved by the lead (2026-10-18, overnight authority).</b></p>
<section id="plain">
  <h2>In plain words</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>The verb:</b> at a faulty machine's panel, look it over with the scanner: the device shows <b>its 3-5 parts</b>, each with a reading (a bar and a word: good, worn, low, failing). Usually one is clearly off. Sometimes two are, and <b>what you saw on the deck</b> (the job says "runs cool"; you saw the door seal gap) tells them apart. You <b>choose</b> the part to fetch.</li>
    <li><b>A wrong pick</b> costs a walk back, never a fail: "Fitted a new seal. Still runs cool: it's the element."</li>
    <li><b>Where it lives:</b> in your locker and on the Works app's Tools page; never in your hands' two slots.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="day">
  <h2>Day 5, Friday</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><time>Morning</time><b>A present from Torres</b><span>Torres is off on Fridays, so he left it for you: Mail at 08:05 from Emeka Halloran, a Works systems officer on shift that day: "Board, when you're in. Zeke left you something. — E.H." At the board Halloran hands you his old scanner with his note taped on: "Mine's older than you. Look after it. Z."</span></li>
    <li><time>The first reading</time><b>With you</b><span>Halloran takes you to a faulty machine held for you (a Tier 1 machine on Deck 3 or 4 with a part cause) and does the first reading aloud ("Element's at twenty. There's your problem"). Then the next one is yours, with Halloran watching: <b>Washer 2</b> in the junior wing's laundry, which turns out to be your first head-scratcher (P3, below).</span></li>
    <li><time>Later the same day</time><b>Your first head-scratcher</b><span>A fault the scanner can't settle on its own (P3, its own page). Then Friday tea.</span></li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section id="panel">
  <h2>The panel</h2>
  <div class="lines">Scanner · Oven 2 (Galley)            the job: runs cool
  Element      ███░░░░░░░  22   failing
  Door seal    ██████░░░░  58   worn
  Fan belt     ████████░░  84   good
                         [ Fetch: element ]  [ Fetch: door seal ]  [ Fetch: fan belt ]</div>
  <ul>
    <li>Readings are machine numbers (like any gauge); <i>your</i> progress is still never a number.</li>
    <li>When two read low, what you see up close (the look-over's line: "cool all over" or "cool by the door") and the Chief's notes ("Cool all over: the element. Cool by the door: the seal.") tell them apart.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="wrong">
  <h2>A wrong pick</h2>
  <p>You fetch the part and fit it; the machine tells you ("Still runs cool: it's the element"), the wrong part goes back on its shelf unused (Tier 1; at Tier 2 a used seal or cartridge is spent), and the job now names the right part. A walk and a few minutes, nothing worse.</p>
</section>

<section id="grow">
  <h2>How it grows</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <div class="card"><b>Stage 1 · Up close</b><span>Read the panel at the machine.</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">Day 5</span></span></div>
    <div class="card"><b>Stage 2 · Across the room</b><span>On your rounds, read a room's machines from its doorway (M1 stage 3), and see a drifting setting before anyone notices (M5 stage 3).</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">after 5 readings</span><span class="tag new">optional</span></span></div>
    <div class="card"><b>Stage 3 · Along a pipe</b><span>As an Officer, it reads flow at a pipe junction (M9 tracing, Step 3).</span><span class="meta"><span class="tag">Officer</span></span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="b" class="builder">
  <h2>For the builder (seat H, sub-block 24g)</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table>
    <tr><th>Section</th><th>What</th><th>Owner</th></tr>
    <tr><td>24g (new)</td><td><code>scanRead(jobId)</code>, the panel view, the pick, the wrong-pick line, the training (ladder row <code>m7</code>), stage 2</td><td>H</td></tr>
    <tr><td>17</td><td><code>scanParts(kind)</code>: the parts of a kind's <code>FAULT_CAUSES</code> part causes (3-5; a kind with no table: just its <code>part</code>, so the panel has one bar and no choice); <code>j.cause</code> (foundation 17.4) says which part is really failing; <code>jobSetPart(jobId, part)</code> replaces the job's first part; <code>returnPart</code> for the unused wrong part (exists)</td><td>S</td></tr>
    <tr><td>15</td><td>the look-over (<code>INSPECT_MINS</code> 3) shows the panel when <code>hasTool('scanner')</code> and the job has a cause; the <code>choose</code> step; at fitting, the wrong-part line and the walk back</td><td>P</td></tr>
    <tr><td>19</td><td>nothing new: the panel is a <code>bars</code> block plus a <code>buttons</code> block in the Works app (or a pop-up view of it during the look-over)</td><td>—</td></tr>
    <tr><td>content</td><td>Halloran's lines (and Torres's and Calder's, for other days), Torres's note (<code>train.m7</code>), the "still…" lines per cause (<code>FAULT_CAUSES</code>' words)</td><td>W</td></tr>
  </table></div>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Readings:</b> the cause's part reads 12-35 ("failing" or "low"); the others 70-96 ("good"), except, with <code>schedU(machSeed(id), day, 874) &lt; .3</code>, one decoy reads 40-60 ("worn"), always one with the same card (<code>shows</code>) but a different <code>sign</code> (<code>fault-tables.html</code>), so what you see up close tells them apart. Exact values from <code>schedU(machSeed(id), day, 875)</code>. Frozen on the job (<code>j.scan</code>) at the first reading, so they don't change on a second look.</li>
    <li><b>The symptom line</b> on the job card comes from the cause's <code>shows</code> ("runs cool", "flickers", "leaks"), shown from Day 2 (real faults), so players learn it before the scanner.</li>
    <li><b>Before the scanner</b> (or with no cause): exactly today's look-over.</li>
    <li><b>Training:</b> Day 5: <code>jobReserve</code> for the teacher (slot 10+, <code>o.train: 'm7'</code>) on a faulty Tier 1 machine with a part cause; they read it (lead), then a second reserved job for you (they follow). The ladder row's <code>by</code> is <code>['torres-zeke', 'halloran-emeka', 'calder']</code>, first on shift wins: on Day 5 (a Friday, Torres's day off: his rota is <code>offDays [3, 4]</code>, Thursday and Friday) it's Emeka Halloran (<code>halloran-emeka</code>, Works systems officer, day shift, off Saturday and Sunday); Calder only if neither is on shift. Lines for all three. <code>toolGive('scanner')</code> at the board. <b>Your (second) reserved job is P3's machine, <code>4-washer-2</code></b>: the teacher's escort (<code>worksEscort</code>, follow) walks you there and <b>doesn't end at the reading</b>: when the reading shows two low parts, the P3 lesson starts on the spot and the escort carries on until the P3 case is called (<code>p3-whats-been-tried.html</code>). P3 is a small row, so it has no escort of its own; it borrows this one.</li>
    <li><b>Wear:</b> <code>toolWear('scanner') += .01</code> per reading (M11 upkeep later; no effect until then).</li>
    <li><b>Notes:</b> <code>simNote('scanned', { machine, right })</code> after the job's done; xp "right part first time" +1 (24.4).</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="save" class="builder">
  <h2>Save</h2>
  <ul><li><code>j.scan = [[part, value], ...]</code> and <code>j.picked</code> on the job; <code>ship.works.tools.scanner</code>; <code>use.m7</code>.</li></ul>
</section>

<section id="tests" class="builder">
  <h2>Tests</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b><code>mech_check</code></b> (24g): every Tier 1 kind with a table has 3-5 parts; the failing part is the cause's and the same twice; two-low cases have different symptoms; the right pick finishes; a wrong pick costs a fetch and returns the part; before the scanner, no choice; readings frozen across save and load.</li>
    <li><b><code>career_check</code></b>: Day 5's training with Halloran (Torres is off) for the steady player, the scanner given.</li>
    <li><b><code>player_check</code></b>: the look-over with and without the scanner.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section id="ranges" class="builder">
  <h2>Builds and keys</h2>
  <ul><li>Seat <b>H</b> (moved from M3 in plan v9 so Step 2 stays at 6 seats), <code>claude/mech-cases</code>, <b>0.55.x</b>. Hash keys <b>874-875</b>.</li></ul>
</section>

<section id="faq">
  <h2>Builders' questions</h2>
  <h3>Torres is off on Day 5 (seat C, 2026-10-18)</h3>
  <p>Torres's rota is <code>offDays [3, 4]</code> (Thursday and Friday), so he can't teach on Day 5. Rows take a <code>by</code> list, first on shift wins: <code>m7</code> and <code>p3</code> are <code>['torres-zeke', 'halloran-emeka', 'calder']</code>, so <b>Emeka Halloran</b> (a Works systems officer on the day shift, off Saturday and Sunday) teaches both on Day 5, handing over Torres's old scanner, which he left with a note; Calder only if neither is on shift (the lead: a Works officer first, Torres always first when he's on). No rota change; the other rows' teachers are on shift on their days (checked: Torres Tue and Mon, Yara Wed, Brennan and Tomas Thu, Calder Mon-Fri). <code>m2</code>'s "oily job" is <code>flag('works.oily')</code>, set by 24b when you turn in an oily job on Day 8 or later.</p>
  <h3>Who walks you to the first puzzle? (seats H and C, through the lead, 2026-10-18)</h3>
  <p>P3 is a <b>small</b> ladder row, and only big rows get a teacher's escort. So <b>P3 borrows the scanner lesson's escort</b>: the scanner lesson's second machine (yours) is <code>4-washer-2</code>, the escort walks you there, and it doesn't end at the reading. The P3 lesson starts on the spot and the escort carries on until the case is called. For this first case only, the first note comes with the job card (handed over at the washer) and the second is on the washer's panel. Later P3 cases follow the normal rule (the first note at the board, the others at the machine).</p>
</section>
